.Dd February 8, 2026
.Dt TTY_DRIVER 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm struct tty_driver
.Nd terminal driver interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/tty.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt struct tty_driver
interface defines the kernel callbacks required to bind a hardware or virtual
terminal device to the TTY core. It provides lifecycle hooks, output paths, and
flow-control integration for canonical and raw line discipline handling.
.Sh FIELDS
.Bl -tag -width "chars_in_buffer"
.It Vt const char *driver_name
Human-readable driver identifier (e.g., "console").
.It Vt const char *name
Base device name (e.g., "tty").
.It Vt int major
Device major number for devfs registrations.
.It Vt int minor_start
Starting minor number for the driver instance range.
.It Vt int num
Total number of devices exported by the driver.
.It Vt int (*install)(struct tty *tty)
Allocate or initialize per-instance driver data. Returns 0 on success.
.It Vt void (*remove)(struct tty *tty)
Release per-instance driver data and resources.
.It Vt int (*open)(struct tty *tty)
Perform hardware initialization when the TTY is opened.
.It Vt void (*close)(struct tty *tty)
Shutdown hardware when the final reference closes.
.It Vt int (*write)(struct tty *tty, const unsigned char *buf, int count)
Write a buffer of output data to the device.
.It Vt int (*put_char)(struct tty *tty, unsigned char c)
Optimized single-character output path.
.It Vt void (*flush_chars)(struct tty *tty)
Kick hardware transmission or drain staged characters.
.It Vt int (*write_room)(struct tty *tty)
Report how many bytes can be accepted by the hardware output path.
.It Vt int (*chars_in_buffer)(struct tty *tty)
Report how many bytes remain pending in the hardware output buffer.
.It Vt int (*ioctl)(struct tty *tty, uint32_t cmd, unsigned long arg)
Driver-specific control operations not handled by the TTY core.
.It Vt void (*set_termios)(struct tty *tty)
Apply termios configuration changes to hardware.
.It Vt void (*throttle)(struct tty *tty)
Engage hardware flow control to pause input.
.It Vt void (*unthrottle)(struct tty *tty)
Release hardware flow control to resume input.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tty 4 ,
.Xr termios 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Vt struct tty_driver
interface first appeared in Substrate.
